    "fanout_notes": [
      "T08 expands into presenter if required, each distinct covering scene, overlays and every planned video first frame; merge all required results before T09.",
      "T13 expands by generated video scene; sourced footage routes to Clip Production without video synthesis.",
      "T11 may execute alongside T07-T10 after the plan exists when the merchant authorized both.",
      "Final assembly waits for all selected scene intervals and final narration alignment.",
      "Feedback can start a separate learning task before T19; T19 is the end-of-delivery consolidation.",
      "Campaign analysis is optional and requires exact ad/export mappings and actual imported measurements; it never blocks ordinary creative delivery.",
      "Video Analysis returns observed media evidence; Reference and Style interprets transfer, Editorial Planning owns the edit schedule, and Independent QA owns its separate verdict.",
      "W01-W13 are the governing workflow map; this task graph only assigns agent ownership to those responsibilities.",
      "Existing approved script/assets and verified reference evidence may satisfy nodes without rerunning production.",
      "Merchant-specific onboarding and platform packaging follow workflow parity; they are not prerequisites for running the harness on our current concepts."
    ],
    "route_scope": "Illustrative authorized full-ad reference route only. Reuse selected inputs and skip satisfied or unrequested tasks; this graph does not define mandatory new workflow stages."
  },
  "state_contract": {
    "task_states": [
      "pending",
